# Independent testability-rubric calibration

Calibrate the instrument used before anchors enter planning or development
gates. The frozen corpus and approved intent are normative. Do not use the
active plan, desired plan verdicts, or already accepted anchors as an oracle.
Requirement form and duplicate preselection are deterministic checks; do not
turn either into a stochastic grammar or provenance-overlap vote.

```json
{
  "schema_version": "2.0.0",
  "operation": "testability",
  "template": {
    "id": "anchor-tuning-testability-request",
    "version": "0.4.1",
    "sha256": {{ template.sha256 | tojson }}
  },
  "correlation_id": {{ correlation_id | tojson }},
  "runtime": {{ runtime | tojson }},
  "authority": {
    "intent": {{ authority.intent | tojson }},
    "anchors": {{ authority.anchors | tojson }}
  },
  "gate": "testability",
  "calibration_corpus": {{ calibration_corpus | tojson }},
  "current_questions": {{ current_questions | tojson }},
  "candidate_minimum": {{ candidate_minimum | tojson }},
  "repeat_count": {{ repeat_count | tojson }},
  "tournament_protocol_version": {{ tournament_protocol_version | tojson }},
  "production_confidence_threshold": {{ production_confidence_threshold | tojson }},
  "confidence_reference_threshold": {{ confidence_reference_threshold | tojson }}
}
```

Freeze cases and expected labels before the first response. Evaluate more
candidates than the released rubric will use, with byte-identical repeat
requests. Every accepted cell needs two confident agreeing answers matching the
oracle; make a third call only when the first two choices disagree. Report
confident `no` or `unclear` as `needs_work`, low-confidence agreement as
`inconclusive`, and unresolved three-way disagreement as `unstable`.
